cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is metadata for a private preparation draft. Cite the immutable release
  commit after the formal repository has been created and released.
title: "Stafford's Conjecture 3.8 for Weyl algebras"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Albert
    given-names: Christopher
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of Stafford's Conjecture 3.8. For every
  characteristic-zero field, every Weyl-algebra rank, and every nonzero d, it
  proves the existence of F, R, and S satisfying 1 = dR + FdS. It also proves
  an exact Bernstein-degree fixed-source strengthening and localization,
  adjoint, differential-operator, evolutionary, and tensor corollaries.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Weyl algebra
  - noncommutative algebra
  - D-module
  - formal mathematics
